	)
	(text "GPIO map (wiring/netlist.py PIN_MAP + wiring/product.py PRODUCT_PINS):\n  GPIO 0  XTAL_32K_P     32.768 kHz crystal (sleep clock for Thread)\n  GPIO 1  XTAL_32K_N     32.768 kHz crystal\n  GPIO 2  HALL_DOOR      Door (DRV5032 OUT)\n  GPIO 3  DRV_nFAULT     Driver fault (open drain)\n  GPIO 4  ENC_B          Motor encoder B\n  GPIO 5  ENC_nEN        Encoder power, active low (strapping pin MTDI: only read in SDIO boot)\n  GPIO 6  VBAT_SENSE     Battery voltage, ADC1 channel 6, through a 4.7M/3.3M divider\n  GPIO 7  LED_R          Status LED red (drives an N-FET)\n  GPIO 8  IO8_PU         Strapping pin: pulled up, so download mode works\n  GPIO 9  BOOT_BTN       Pairing / reset button, and BOOT (download mode if held at reset)\n  GPIO12  USB_DM         USB D- (programming header)\n  GPIO13  USB_DP         USB D+ (programming header)\n  GPIO14  LED_G          Status LED green\n  GPIO15  LED_B          Status LED blue (strapping pin: ignored unless the JTAG-select eFuse is burned)\n  GPIO18  MOT_IN1        Motor A in 1 (PWM)\n  GPIO19  MOT_IN2        Motor A in 2 (PWM)\n  GPIO20  DRV_nSLEEP     Driver enable\n  GPIO21  ENC_A          Motor encoder A\n  GPIO22  HALL_LOCKED    Bolt locked (DRV5032 OUT)\n  GPIO23  HALL_UNLOCKED  Bolt unlocked (DRV5032 OUT)\n  GPIO16/17 UART0 TX/RX to J3\n\nOpen items:\n  - D1 has no footprint: Kingbright APTF1616 is not in KiCad's library.\n  - L1: check the 1008 footprint against Murata's DFE252012PD land pattern.\n  - J1: check the Pololu SH-style cable in a genuine JST SM06B-SRSS-TB.\n  - J2: check which pin the battery lead's red wire lands on.\n  - C1: size the bulk cap on the dev kit (motor stall on cold, aging cells).\n  - GPIO15 (LED_B) is a strapping pin, ignored unless the JTAG-select eFuse is burned.\n  - Antenna: module end over the board edge, or a copper keep-out under it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 440 200 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "44ce58bf-d364-5852-9d46-a0285dd89025")
	)
